function [Sf,freq] = PSDmodel(num,den,var,Nf,fs)
% [Sf,freq] = PSDmodel(num,den,var,Nf,fs) computes the Power Spectral Density (PSD) 
% of the AutoRegressive (AR) model described by the numerator coefficients (num), 
% denominator coefficients (den), and variance (var). 
% Nf is the number of frequency points to compute, and fs is the sampling frequency.
%
% The function uses the freqz function to calculate the frequency response of the 
% digital filter defined by the given numerator and denominator coefficients. 
% It then computes the magnitude of the frequency response and scales it by the 
% variance to obtain the PSD. The output Sf represents the computed PSD values, 
% while freq contains the corresponding frequency points.

[H, omega] = freqz(num, den, Nf, fs);
H = abs(H);
Sf = var * H.^2;
freq = omega;

end

